ROMS basic usage:
-----------------

Instructions for installing, compiling and running ROMS are in the
documentation at https://cworthy-ucla-roms.readthedocs.io (source in docs/).

Directories:
------------

   src/           - The ROMS source code.
                    Don't edit it for a simulation: compile each configuration
                    in its own directory, whose files override the ones in src/.

   Examples/      - The Iceland nested-simulation example used by the tutorials.

   Work/          - A Makefile to copy into a new configuration directory.

   Tools-Roms/    - Pre- and post-processing tools (partit, ncjoin, mpc, ...).
                    Build them once with "make" in this directory.

   environments/  - Environment scripts for supported HPC systems, and the
                    files that build the CI containers.

   tests/         - The pytest regression suite (see tests/README.md).

   docs/          - Source of the documentation site.

   ci/            - Helper scripts for continuous integration (see ci/README).

Less relevant: (you're unlikely to use these)

   New-tools/     - Partitioning tools for land-masked MPI tilings
                    (MPI_MASKING), with their own Makefile.

   NHMG/          - Non-hydrostatic modules (unmaintained).

   Documentation/ - Historical notes from upstream UCLA ROMS; not maintained.
